"use strict";(self.webpackChunk_N_E=self.webpackChunk_N_E||[]).push([[15257],{15257:function(e){e.exports=JSON.parse('{"content":"\\n<center>\\n<TvCard\\n  cover=\\"/assets/snippets/screen/trueeducation2026.jpg\\"\\n  title=\\"True Education (2026)\\"\\n  release_date=\\"2026-06-05\\"\\n  episode_count=10\\n  genres=[\\"Action\\"]\\n  rating=3\\n  tags=\\"tv\\"\\n/>\\n</center>\\n\\n## Review\\nI started watching casually, having seen it circulate so much on `Netflix` and `social media`.\\n\\nThe overall content and flow is very <mark>simple and intuitive</mark>.  \\nBeing based on a <mark>webtoon</mark>, I think this directness stands out even more.  \\nThe pacing is also very fast.\\n\\nThese days, people seem to struggle if the story is even slightly complex or long.  \\nIt probably comes from being so accustomed to fast-paced media like `short-form` content.  \\nDramas used to be produced in `16-episode` or even `20-episode` runs,  \\nbut now the trend seems to be `12 episodes` on the longer end and `8 episodes` on the shorter end.  \\nAs someone who personally enjoys complex and nuanced stories, I find this trend a bit disappointing.\\n```adcard\\n```\\nI\'ve personally thought that the <mark>collapse of teachers\' authority</mark> is a serious problem.  \\nThis isn\'t just a student issue — it\'s a problem involving teachers, parents, and the entire social system,  \\nand I\'ve felt that if things continue, it could spiral into a situation that\'s impossible to reverse.  \\n\\nBecause a reality where <mark>true education</mark> can be enforced directly as in this drama cannot exist, the show leaves a somewhat bitter aftertaste.  \\nPerhaps that\'s why each of the protagonist\'s satisfying action scenes brought catharsis and a sense of emptiness at the same time.\\n\\nSince I don\'t care for forced `bad endings`, I think wrapping up with a <mark>happy ending</mark> like this is not a bad choice.  \\nIt carries a heavy and realistic message, but at least the ending lands with satisfying resolution.\\n"}')}}]);